In financial applications, after a "Maker" uploads and processes 50,000 rows, a "Checker" must review and approve it. Your original service had this approval logic mixed in with everything else. We need to isolate it so that if your business requirements change (e.g., adding a second level of approval), you only have to touch one file.

### 4. `VoucherWorkflowEngine.java` (The State Machine)

Create this file in your `Service.core` package. Its sole responsibility is managing the lifecycle of a batch (Approve, Reject, Cancel) and maintaining the audit trail so compliance teams are happy.

```java
package com.fincore.VoucherService.Service.core;

import com.fincore.VoucherService.Models.RequestVoucher;
import com.fincore.VoucherService.Models.VoucherWorkflow;
import com.fincore.VoucherService.Repository.RequestVoucherRepository;
import com.fincore.VoucherService.Repository.VoucherWorkflowRepository;
import com.fincore.VoucherService.Exception.CustomExceptions;
import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional;

import java.time.LocalDateTime;

@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class VoucherWorkflowEngine {

    private final RequestVoucherRepository requestVoucherRepository;
    private final VoucherWorkflowRepository voucherWorkflowRepository;

    @Transactional
    public void processWorkflowAction(String batchId, String action, String userId, String remarks) {
        log.info("WORKFLOW_ACTION | Batch: {} | Action: {} | User: {}", batchId, action, userId);

        RequestVoucher batch = requestVoucherRepository.findById(batchId)
                .orElseThrow(() -> new CustomExceptions.ResourceNotFoundException("Batch not found: " + batchId));

        // 1. Authorization & State Check
        validateActionAllowance(batch, action, userId);

        // 2. Apply State Transition
        String previousState = batch.getStatus();
        switch (action.toUpperCase()) {
            case "APPROVE":
                batch.setStatus("APPROVED_READY_FOR_EXECUTION");
                break;
            case "REJECT":
                batch.setStatus("REJECTED_BY_CHECKER");
                break;
            case "CANCEL":
                batch.setStatus("CANCELLED_BY_MAKER");
                break;
            default:
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unknown workflow action: " + action);
        }

        requestVoucherRepository.save(batch);

        // 3. Record Audit Trail
        logWorkflowAction(batchId, action, userId, remarks, previousState, batch.getStatus());
    }

    private void validateActionAllowance(RequestVoucher batch, String action, String userId) {
        // Standard Maker/Checker Rule: Maker cannot approve their own batch
        if (("APPROVE".equalsIgnoreCase(action) || "REJECT".equalsIgnoreCase(action)) 
                && userId.equals(batch.getCreatedBy())) {
            log.error("WORKFLOW_VIOLATION | Batch: {} | User {} attempted to approve/reject own batch", batch.getBatchId(), userId);
            throw new IllegalStateException("Maker cannot approve or reject their own batch.");
        }

        // State machine rules
        if ("PENDING_CHECKER_APPROVAL".equals(batch.getStatus()) && "CANCEL".equalsIgnoreCase(action)) {
             // Let's assume a Maker can cancel before it's approved
             if (!userId.equals(batch.getCreatedBy())) {
                 throw new IllegalStateException("Only the Maker can cancel a pending batch.");
             }
        }
    }

    private void logWorkflowAction(String batchId, String action, String userId, String remarks, String oldState, String newState) {
        VoucherWorkflow auditLog = new VoucherWorkflow();
        auditLog.setBatchIdFk(batchId);
        auditLog.setAction(action.toUpperCase());
        auditLog.setActionBy(userId);
        auditLog.setRemarks(remarks);
        auditLog.setPreviousState(oldState);
        auditLog.setNewState(newState);
        auditLog.setActionAt(LocalDateTime.now());
        
        voucherWorkflowRepository.save(auditLog);
    }
}

```

### 5. `VoucherQueryService.java` (The Read-Only Layer)

You also need a place to put all those `GET` requests that fetch data for your React UI (e.g., getting the summary of pending batches). Create this file in `Service.core`.

By making this a separate file, you ensure that heavy database reads don't block the same file that does heavy database writes.

```java
package com.fincore.VoucherService.Service.core;

import com.fincore.VoucherService.Models.RequestVoucher;
import com.fincore.VoucherService.Models.VoucherWorkflow;
import com.fincore.VoucherService.Repository.RequestVoucherRepository;
import com.fincore.VoucherService.Repository.VoucherWorkflowRepository;
import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

import java.util.List;

@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class VoucherQueryService {

    private final RequestVoucherRepository requestVoucherRepository;
    private final VoucherWorkflowRepository voucherWorkflowRepository;

    public List<RequestVoucher> getPendingBatchesForChecker() {
        return requestVoucherRepository.findAllByStatus("PENDING_CHECKER_APPROVAL");
    }

    public List<RequestVoucher> getBatchesByMaker(String userId) {
        return requestVoucherRepository.findAllByCreatedBy(userId);
    }

    public List<VoucherWorkflow> getWorkflowHistory(String batchId) {
        // From your original code snippet:
        return voucherWorkflowRepository.findByBatchIdFkOrderByLastActionAtAsc(batchId);
    }
    
    public RequestVoucher getBatchSummaryDetails(String batchId) {
        return requestVoucherRepository.findById(batchId).orElse(null);
    }
}

